--TEST--
`Countable`, `ArrayAccess`, `IteratorAggregate`, `Traversable` and `Generator` are not declared, so naming one in an `implements` clause or in a type position is a compile error — `rule:iteration/no-magic-collection-interfaces`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:iteration/what-does-not-exist
class Sized implements Countable {}

class Indexed implements ArrayAccess {}

class Aggregate implements IteratorAggregate {}

class Walked implements Traversable {}

// The same refusal reaches a type position: `Generator` is not a name a program may write,
// even though a method with `yield` is what PHP would call one.
class Steps {
    public static function take(Generator $g): void {}
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Countable` is not declared
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
